      "explanation": "A minus sign before parentheses reverses the sign of every enclosed term. Simplify each bracket first, then subtract:\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\n[x-(y-x)]-[(x-y)-x]\n&=(x-y+x)-(x-y-x)\\\\\n&=(2x-y)-(-y)\\\\\n&=2x-y+y\\\\\n&=2x.\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\boxed{2x}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
      "id": "1986_AMC_12_Q01_m1",
